zebkit @VERSION@
https://github.com/ikey4u/zebkit

zebkit is free software: you can redistribute it and/or modify it under the
terms of the GNU Lesser General Public License as published by the Free
Software Foundation, either version 2.1 of the License, or (at your option)
any later version. The license is in LICENSE.

It contains Chromium @CHROMIUM@ and the third-party libraries Chromium and
zebkit use (among them Blink, V8, Skia, PDFium, FFmpeg, ICU, SQLite and
BoringSSL), each under its own license. THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt lists every
one of them with its license text.

The source of this build is the zebkit repository at tag v@VERSION@:

    https://github.com/ikey4u/zebkit/tree/v@VERSION@

It names the Chromium release the engine is built from (upstream.lock), the
changes made to it (patches/) and how it is built (scripts/, profiles/).
FFmpeg is built with its LGPL parts only: no GPL and no nonfree component.

An application uses the engine as a shared library (libzebkit.so.1,
Zebkit.framework or zebkit.dll), which it can replace with another build of
the same version. docs/LICENSING.md in the repository says what shipping the
engine with an application involves.

